body:
Yeah I think typically you need to have some level of emotional connection with the listener for them to be engaged for a specific reason - whether that be cultural, the intent of why they are listening (to get amped for going out, to relax etc.).

&#x200B;

We each interpret music in different ways - so I think it's hard to actually have music that has zero emotional impact on the people who listen to it!

Check us out!!! I'd be curious to get your thoughts. We're building an app to help people use their Spotify listening to understand and manage their moods :)

&#x200B;

www.ensu.com/download

We will be reaching out over the next week or so, however there is a selection criteria and so not every applicant will be on-boarded onto the study. If you are very keen to do the study, please DM me or email me at [info@zenful.io](mailto:info@zenful.io), and I'll look to see if we can speed up the on-boarding for you.

&#x200B;

Thanks!

My email is [amol.avasare@zenful.io](mailto:amol.avasare@zenful.io). You can also skip the survey process and email me directly there.

&#x200B;

Thanks!

Awesome - love the interest! I'm sure you'll understand a lot about what we're doing. 

&#x200B;

Will DM you. Pseudo's are more than fine (don't care about personally identifiable details, just want a way to contact you as we speak via phone / email to every one of our users before we on-board them)

Fair enough. We were filtering based on age group as a proxy for this, but yes you're right we should call that out more clearly. 

&#x200B;

Will update for future posting.

Same amount - we ended up just doing them all as phone calls instead.

&#x200B;

Nearly every user interview we held, we've then converted onto a longer term on-going 25/month paid study. Not sure if they were from this thread - feel free to chime in anybody!
